message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite both the software artifact and the paper below."
title: "RustRedis: a Redis-compatible in-memory key-value server for measuring per-command observability overhead"
abstract: >-
  RustRedis is a Redis-compatible in-memory key-value server written in Rust,
  instrumented with eight interchangeable per-command metrics collectors chosen
  so that adjacent pairs differ along exactly one design axis (synchronization
  discipline, metric key cardinality, aggregation locality, per-sample payload).
  The repository contains the server, the load generator, the Randomized
  Multiple Interleaved Trials experiment runner, the raw data from 29,520
  benchmark runs on fourteen dedicated Azure virtual machines, and the analysis
  and figure code that regenerates every number in the accompanying paper.
